{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1104490-could-these-antagonists-work-in-changeling","id":1104490,"title":"Could these antagonists work in Changeling?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-16T14:50:27-07:00","id":1104490,"title":"Could these antagonists work in Changeling?","content":"I am thinking about getting C20 when it comes out and i already came up with a setting. That setting is Winterberry, a town in Maine that is plagued with a crime wave. The setting has two gangs, The Winterberry Overlords and the 9th Avenue Skulls. The Overlords, the biggest of the two are led by a Unseelie Redcap named Arnold Hastings. Hastings is a reincarnation of a Red Cap Rum Runner by the name of Big Lou Lombardi who buried his loot in a coastal cave along the town's coastline. After becoming a changeling, Hastings came back to town to find his past lives' loot, but could not remember where he put it. So, he took over the Overlords and is using the gang to occupy himself while looking for Big Lou's treasure.<br /> <br /> The 9th Avenue Skulls are a French-Canadian gang that came to town rather recently and immediately began antagonizing the Overlords. No one has actually seen the leader of the Skulls. In fact, no one even know who exactly the leader is or if he is even in the States. The only man who can claim to be the leader is Jean-Claude <span style=\"font-family:Roboto, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Moreau, a recent immigrant of French ethnicity and a local troublemaker. Among the local Changeling gossip circles are many outlandish about the Skulls and their leader. Some of these rumors are that Jean-Claude is actually a vampire all the way to the idea that a Unseelie Sidhe is secretly bankrolling the Skulls. There is one more sinister rumor that is rarely spoken of however, Changelings that know about them claim that House Balor is secretly backing the gang.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Both gangs are at a state of active warfare and are tearing the peaceful town of Winterberry apart. They are both waiting for the date of October 5th, 1985, the towns bicentennial celebration to plan something big, something which they hope will turn the tables on the other.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">So my question is how would you make these gang's work in this setting. I was personally thinking of making the player character's younger and in less control of their powers which would make the mainly human gangster's both a bigger threat and more likely to cause big problems for the PC's. But what say you.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 06-16-2017, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}